{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good afternoon, Thomas, just to confirm full name and date of birth.",
   "start": 0.05,
   "end": 4.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thomas Nowak, November 30th, 1985.",
   "start": 5.17,
   "end": 8.61
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Perfect, it's been about three months since we started the acetalopram. How are things?",
   "start": 10.02,
   "end": 14.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Better, I'd say. Maybe halfway better. I'm not lying awake every night anymore, but the worrying is still there most days.",
   "start": 14.76,
   "end": 21.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "What does the worrying look like these days?",
   "start": 22.44,
   "end": 24.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "mostly work. I'm a loan officer at Lakeshore Credit Union and there's a reorganization going on, and my wife Kaja is due in November, so, you know, there's a lot on my mind. My shoulders are tight all the time and I snap at people more than I want to.",
   "start": 24.26,
   "end": 41.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Congratulations on the baby, and how's falling asleep?",
   "start": 42.32,
   "end": 45.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Still takes me maybe 45 minutes most nights. My brain just won't shut off.",
   "start": 45.88,
   "end": 51.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "You were having panic attacks back in the spring, any since we last met?",
   "start": 51.06,
   "end": 55.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, none since April. That part's actually gone.",
   "start": 56.14,
   "end": 58.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's great, remind me what dose of acetaloprem you're on.",
   "start": 59.46,
   "end": 62.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "The five milligrams? Oh no, wait, sorry. I went up to ten after the first two weeks like you said, so ten every morning.",
   "start": 62.82,
   "end": 70.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "OK, ten milligrams. Any side effects, nausea, sexual side effects, anything like that?",
   "start": 71.34,
   "end": 76.44
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, nothing really. Stomach was a bit off the first week, then fine.",
   "start": 76.44,
   "end": 81.64
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And the hydroxyzine. The 25 milligrams for bad moments. How often are you using it?",
   "start": 82.42,
   "end": 87.44
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Maybe twice in the last month. It works, but it knocks me out.",
   "start": 88.24,
   "end": 92.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Anything else you're taking, over -the -counter or supplements?",
   "start": 92.5,
   "end": 95.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Magnesium glycinate. 200 milligrams at night. A friend recommended it.",
   "start": 96.52,
   "end": 101.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's fine to keep. How much coffee are you drinking? Ah, honestly,",
   "start": 102.28,
   "end": 106.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "four cups a day. Maybe five on bad days.",
   "start": 106.56,
   "end": 109.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That might be feeding the jitters a bit, any alcohol.",
   "start": 110.08,
   "end": 112.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A beer on the weekend, that's it.",
   "start": 113.6,
   "end": 115.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I have to ask this every time. Any thoughts of suicide or of harming yourself? No, none. Good, so your GAD7 today is 12. When you started it was 16, so it's moving in the right direction, but it's still in the moderate range. Your blood pressure is 128 over 82 and your pulse is 84. You look a little tense but you're talkative, your mood is anxious,",
   "start": 115.9,
   "end": 137.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "your thinking is clear. Yeah, tense is a good word for it.",
   "start": 138.12,
   "end": 142.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So I think this is generalised anxiety disorder that's partly responding. You're tolerating the acetalopram well, so I'd like to increase it to 20mg once a day. Take two of your tense until the new prescription is filled.",
   "start": 142.74,
   "end": 155.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, that's easy.",
   "start": 156.04,
   "end": 157.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the hydroxyzine for the rough moments up to once a day and don't drive after you take it. Keep the magnesium. And I'd like you to cut the coffee to two cups a day, nothing afternoon.",
   "start": 158.06,
   "end": 168.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That one's going to hurt, but okay.",
   "start": 168.86,
   "end": 171.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Are you still seeing the therapist for CBT?",
   "start": 171.52,
   "end": 173.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Every other week, yes.",
   "start": 174.56,
   "end": 175.86
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good, keep that going. And as always, if you ever have thoughts of hurting yourself, call or text 988 right away. I'd like to see you back in six weeks, so that's around November 4th before the baby comes.",
   "start": 176.42,
   "end": 188.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sounds good. Can you send the summary to my portal? My email changed. It's tamas .noac .fasmil .com.",
   "start": 188.52,
   "end": 197.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'll update it, take care, and good luck with the reorganisation.",
   "start": 197.58,
   "end": 200.94
  }
 ],
